  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["J11"],
      "pins": ["J11.A6", "J11.A7", "J11.B6", "J11.B7"],
      "nets": ["NET0001", "NET0025"],
      "obs": "On the USB sheet, the USB‑C receptacle J11 (USB_C_Receptacle_USB2.0) has its two D+ pins split across opposite nets and its two D‑ pins split across opposite nets: pin A7 (D+) and pin B6 (D‑) both carry NET0001, while pin B7 (D‑) and pin A6 (D+) both carry NET0025. Thus each net contains one D+ and one D‑ pin of the connector.",
      "expected": "For a USB‑C receptacle the duplicate differential pins must be paired by function: A7 and A6 (both D+) tied to the D+ net, and B7 and B6 (both D‑) tied to the D‑ net (e.g. NET0001/NET0025 = D+/D‑ respectively), so that the cable‑side pairing presents a clean differential pair to the FT231XS.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "USB sheet, J11 USB_C_Receptacle_USB2.0: A7 D+ = NET0001, B7 D‑ = NET0025, A6 D+ = NET0025, B6 D‑ = NET0001"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Power distribution: ... USB input \"OR‑ing\"/protection circuitry ... (the USB device path through U1 FT231XS and J11 is the intended USB serial interface)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The USB‑C device port's D+ and D‑ lines are cross‑bridged through the receptacle's duplicate pins (NET0001 shorts one D+ to one D‑, and NET0025 shorts the other D+ to the other D‑). When a cable is inserted the differential pair is shorted together, so enumeration/communication on the FT231XS USB port fails (and the 27R series terminations R50/R15 do not protect against the cross).",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most of the board matches the specification (16 MHz CAN crystals Y3/Y6, MCP2515 SPI sharing with separate CS, SM712‑style CAN TVS, LTC4412 ideal‑diode controller, ISL54222 analog switches, e‑stop sink buffers feeding ESTOP_OUT/NET0017 on the CAN connectors), and the designator renumbering versus the spec is expected for a different build. The one deviation I can read off the drawing is on the USB‑C device receptacle J11, where the duplicate D+/D‑ pins are cross‑tied (A7+B6 on NET0001, B7+A6 on NET0025), bridging the USB differential pair; my pin‑label reading confidence is moderate, so the verdict is reported with reduced confidence."
}

